# SYNFLOX Backend Development Rules

You are a .NET Clean Architecture expert working on the SYNFLOX Central Licensing System.

## Project Context
- SYNFLOX is a Central Licensing System for managing enterprise product licenses
- Uses Clean Architecture with 4 layers: Domain → Application → Infrastructure → WebAPI
- Supports multi-language (English/Arabic) with localization
- Uses JWT authentication for Admin access only
- All IDs are encrypted in responses, decrypted in requests
- Implements soft delete pattern with audit trails

## Architecture Rules
- Follow Clean Architecture strictly: Domain has NO dependencies
- Application layer depends ONLY on Domain
- Infrastructure depends on Domain and Application
- WebAPI depends on all layers
- Separate entity CRUD from business operations (SRP principle)
- Use repository pattern with Unit of Work
- All entities extend AuditEntity<Guid> for audit trails

## Feature Implementation Order
1. Domain: Entity → Repository Interface → Enums/Exceptions
2. Application: DTOs → Service Interface → AutoMapper Profile
3. Infrastructure: Repository → Service → EF Configuration → Registration
4. WebAPI: Controller → Authorization → Validation → Error Handling

## ID Encryption Rules
- CRITICAL: Encryption/Decryption ONLY in AutoMapper converters
- Services work ONLY with decrypted GUIDs internally
- Controllers can decrypt route parameters (boundary layer)
- Use EncryptGuidConverter for Entity → DTO
- Use DecryptGuidConverter for DTO → Entity
- NEVER manually encrypt/decrypt in services

## Authorization & Validation
- Use [Authorize(Policy = "SuperAdminOnly")] for management endpoints
- Use [AllowAnonymous] only for public status checks
- Always check ModelState.IsValid on POST/PUT
- Throw BadRequestException/NotFoundException with localized messages
- Use _localizer["Key"] for all user-facing messages

## Database Rules
- Create IEntityTypeConfiguration<Entity> for each entity
- Add proper indexes (unique, composite, filtered)
- Always filter by !IsDeleted in custom queries
- Use _unitOfWork.SaveChangesAsync() after operations
- Configure string lengths and constraints

## Localization
- Add keys to SharedResource.resx (EN) and SharedResource.ar.resx (AR)
- Use format: {Feature}.{Action} (e.g., "Company.Created")
- Support Accept-Language header, X-Language header, or ?lang= parameter
- Default to English if no language specified

## What NOT to Do
- Mix entity CRUD with business operations in same service
- Skip ID encryption/decryption
- Use hardcoded strings instead of localization
- Access database directly from controllers
- Forget ModelState validation or authorization
- Create entities that don't extend AuditEntity
- Manual encrypt/decrypt in services (use mappers only)

## Code Quality
- Use PascalCase for entities, services, controllers
- Add XML documentation to public interfaces
- One class per file, file name matches class name
- Inject dependencies through constructor using interfaces
- Keep business logic in service layer, not controllers
